w well-known, stable peers that new nodes can connect to initially to join the network and discover other peers via the DHT.\n\n**Architectural Overview:**\n\n```\nUSER\u0027S MACHINE:\n+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Browser (Frontend - HTML, CSS, JS - Insta UI)     |\n|   \u003c-- HTTP/WebSocket --\u003e                          |\n+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Local Python App (Backend - FastAPI/Flask)        |\n|   - Serves Frontend                               |\n|   - API for UI (search, post, dm, profile)        |\n|   - Manages Local Data Store (SQLite, files)      |\n|   - Runs libp2p Node                              |\n|     +-----------------------------------------+   |\n|     | libp2p Node                             |   |\n|     |   - Peer Identity (Keypair, PeerID)     |   |\n|     |   - DHT (Kademlia) for discovery/nametags|   |\n|     |   - PubSub for real-time updates        |   |\n|     |   - Stream Muxing (Mplex)               |   |\n|     |   - Data Sync (CRDTs logic)             |   |\n|     |   - Connects to Bootstrap \u0026 Other Peers |   |\n|     +-----------------------------------------+   |\n+---------------------------------------------------+\n      ^ |\n      | | (libp2p network protocols)\n      v |\n+---------------------------------------------------+\n| Other P2P Peers / Bootstrap Nodes                 |\n+---------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n**Evolution of Your Code:**\n\nLet\u0027s see how your existing files fit or need to change:\n\n*   **`client.py` / `server.py` (libp2p based):**\n    *   **Good:** This is the right P2P library.\n    *   **Evolve:** Instead of a client/server, you\u0027ll have one `P2PNode` class that can both listen and connect. It will integrate DHT and PubSub functionalities from `libp2p`.\n    *   The concept of connecting to a specific `server_id` will change to discovering peers via DHT or connecting to bootstrap nodes.\n\n* 