der a Node.js backend) which has very mature DHT support, or contribute to/rely on the community for `libp2p-python`\u0027s DHT.\n*   **CRDTs:** Choosing the right CRDTs and implementing their synchronization logic correctly.\n*   **Scalability of PubSub:** Global PubSub can be noisy. You\u0027ll need topic scoping (e.g., `user/\u003cpeerID\u003e/profile_updates`, `hashtags/\u003ctag\u003e`).\n*   **Data Persistence and Availability:** Peers are not always online. How do you ensure data remains available? (e.g., encouraging users to run nodes, \"pinning\" services, or relying on high-uptime peers).\n*   **UI Complexity:** Replicating Instagram\u0027s UI is a huge task.\n\nThis is a marathon, not a sprint. Start with the core P2P communication and local server, then gradually add features. The existing `libp2p` code is a great starting point for the P2P layer. Good luck!",
